Subject: [PATCH] libbe: don't adopt the roster's looper port after exec()

When the roster launches an application it pre-registers the new team and
creates a looper port for it, owned by that team. BApplication then drops
its own port and adopts the roster's. That breaks when the file launched is
a script that exec()s the real application -- R Chromium, R Twitter and
the other web-app launchers do exactly that: exec() deletes every port the
team owns, so the BApplication built after it adopts a port that no longer
exists. task_looper() then retries the failing read forever, and the app's
main thread uses a whole CPU core in port_count()/port_buffer_size_etc()
returning B_BAD_PORT_ID, while messages to the application are lost.

Only adopt the roster's port if it is still alive and owned by this team;
otherwise keep the looper's own port. The registrar records whatever port
CompleteRegistration() reports, so nothing else needs to change.

diff --git a/src/kits/app/Application.cpp b/src/kits/app/Application.cpp
index 8620dbdcc8..51dec0a4bd 100644
--- a/src/kits/app/Application.cpp
+++ b/src/kits/app/Application.cpp
@@ -432,8 +432,15 @@ BApplication::_InitData(const char* signature, bool initGUI, status_t* _error)
 	if (preRegistered) {
 		// we are pre-registered => the app info has been filled in
 		// Check whether we need to replace the looper port with a port
-		// created by the roster.
-		if (appInfo.port >= 0 && appInfo.port != fMsgPort) {
+		// created by the roster. The roster gives that port to the team it
+		// launched, and exec() deletes a team's ports: an app started by a
+		// launcher script that exec()s it would adopt a dead port and spin
+		// in task_looper() on B_BAD_PORT_ID. Keep our own port then; the
+		// registrar takes whatever port CompleteRegistration() reports.
+		port_info portInfo;
+		if (appInfo.port >= 0 && appInfo.port != fMsgPort
+			&& get_port_info(appInfo.port, &portInfo) == B_OK
+			&& portInfo.team == team) {
 			delete_port(fMsgPort);
 			fMsgPort = appInfo.port;
 		} else
